   "date": "2026-11-22",
   "html": "<p><strong>What</strong></p><ul><li><code>docs/</code>: a static GitHub Pages site, DBZ-flavoured but scientific. The landing page covers the goals, the three fighters, the FusionDance diagram, the three budgets, the big ideas and the training-arc roadmap. The devlog page has the experiment log with status filters, a val-loss \"power level\" chart, and the version timeline.</li><li><code>experiments/experiments.json</code>: a registry of the nine planned arcs (E0–E8), from the baseline to self-speculative decoding.</li><li><code>tools/build_site_data.py</code>: generates <code>docs/data/site-data.js</code> from <code>DEVLOG.md</code> plus the registry, so the site can't drift from the devlog.</li><li><code>.gitignore</code>: <code>data/</code> → <code>/data/</code> (root only), because it was also hiding <code>docs/data/</code>.</li></ul><p><strong>Results</strong>: n/a. Site checked in the browser at desktop and phone widths: no console errors, no horizontal scroll.</p><p><strong>Decisions</strong>: The site reads generated JS data (not fetched JSON), so it also works when opened from disk. Experiment status is tracked in the registry, not in prose.</p><p><strong>Next</strong>: push to GitHub and enable Pages (main, <code>/docs</code>) when ready; then WSL setup and E0.</p>"
